  "body": "Hello. I need a mechanism to deny mobile client for some user. I tried to delete unexpected Android device by script\r\n\r\nFist I get device list \r\nsqlite3 /mnt/database/homeserver.db 'select user_id,device_id,ip,user_agent,last_seen from user_ips;' | grep 'Android'\r\n\r\nThen I take Device ID and follow instruction\r\nhttps://matrix.org/docs/spec/client_server/r0.6.0#post-matrix-client-r0-delete-devices\r\n\r\ncurl -X DELETE 'http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/r0/devices/$DEVICE?access_token='$TOKEN''\r\nwhere $DEVICE is variable from user_ips tables and $TOKEN from \r\n\r\ncurl -XPOST  -d '{\"type\":\"m.login.password\", \"user\":\"@username:DOMAIN\", \"password\":\"password\"}' \"http://localhost:8008/_matrix/client/r0/login\r\n\r\nAND NOTHING HAPPENED\r\n{\"session\":\"OTYGvoepxcKsSVqlLsBHxgEG\",\"flows\":[{\"stages\":[\"m.login.password\"]}],\"params\":{}}",
